{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T22:36:17Z","input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_tokens":100131,"output_tokens":4846,"thinking":"The MikroTik configuration shows `ether1` as the internet input (WAN) and a `bridge-LAN` comprising ports `ether2` through `ether5`, assigned to the `192.168.15.0/24` network. The gateway is `192.168.15.1`. This network information will be crucial for understanding the overall network setup.\n\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nNetwork configuration details were examined to determine the available methods for managing bandwidth.  Multiple approaches emerged for assigning specific bandwidth tiers to network clients, including DHCP lease configuration and address-list based rules. Address-list-based methods with firewall mangling and queue tree were identified as a streamlined option.\n\n\nPPPoE and Hotspot profiles for different bandwidth tiers (5, 10, 20, 30, and 40 Mbps) are being created to support connections from devices like LiteBeam M5/PowerBeam M5.  The script will ensure FastTrack is disabled in the firewall to enable proper speed limiting via Simple Queues and Queue Trees.  Finally, the ready-to-use configuration file will be saved in two specified locations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# ==============================================================================\\n# PLANTILLA 06: PAQUETES DE INTERNET DE 5, 10, 20, 30 Y 40 MEGAS EN MIKROTIK\\n# Compatible con RouterOS v6 y v7 (Red 192.168.15.x, Antenas Ubiquiti y PPPoE)\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# QUÉ HACE ESTE SCRIPT:\\n# 1. Desactiva FastTrack en el Firewall (si está activo, las colas no limitan).\\n# 2. Crea los Tipos de Cola PCQ (Per Connection Queue) para 5M, 10M, 20M, 30M y 40M\\n#    para que cada cliente reciba exactamente su paquete de forma individual.\\n# 3. Crea las Simple Queues para controlar clientes por IP fija o por rangos en\\n#    tu red 192.168.15.x:\\n#      - PAQUETE  5 MEGAS ( 5M Bajada /  5M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.50  - 192.168.15.89\\n#      - PAQUETE 10 MEGAS (10M Bajada / 10M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.90  - 192.168.15.129\\n#      - PAQUETE 20 MEGAS (20M Bajada / 20M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.130 - 192.168.15.169\\n#      - PAQUETE 30 MEGAS (30M Bajada / 30M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.170 - 192.168.15.209\\n#      - PAQUETE 40 MEGAS (40M Bajada / 40M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.210 - 192.168.15.250\\n# 4. Incluye plantillas individuales por IP (con Ráfaga/Burst opcional) y también\\n#    los 5 Perfiles PPPoE listos por si autenticas antenas LiteBeam/PowerBeam.\\n# ==============================================================================\\n\\n{\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PASO 1: ASEGURAR QUE FASTTRACK ESTÉ DESACTIVADO PARA QUE LAS COLAS FUNCIONEN\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n/ip firewall filter remove [find action=\\\"fasttrack-connection\\\"]\\n\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PASO 2: CREAR COLAS INTELIGENTES PCQ (CADA IP DENTRO DEL PAQUETE RECIBE SU VELOCIDAD)\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n/queue type remove [find name~\\\"PCQ_PAQUETE_\\\"]\\n\\n# --- \n<truncated 6730 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\microtik\\\\microtik\\\\00_Plantillas_RSC_Listas_Para_Usar\\\\06_paquetes_internet_5_10_20_30_40_megas.rsc\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
